      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The bridge earned its name from its builder, Witmer, who was a local entrepreneur in the early 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lancasterhistory.org/witmers-bridge/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lightner Witmer, born in Philadelphia in 1867, is credited with founding the field of clinical psychology.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightner_Witmer",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1907 Witmer launched The Psychological Clinic, the first journal devoted entirely to clinical psychology.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightner_Witmer",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Witmer opened the world’s first speech clinic in 1914, pioneering early intervention for language disorders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightner_Witmer",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town of Witmer, Pennsylvania, grew around the historic bridge and remains a quiet reminder of early American engineering.",
